WEBVTT

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:09.940
AUGUST 9, 2095 - MONOLITH CODE - ROOKIE EVENT

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.370
Morisaki!

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.990
What is this?

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:15.410
What happened here?

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:19.040
Battering Ram, a Rank A Lethal Spell.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:20.750
On top of that, they jumped the gun.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:23.000
That's totally against the rules!

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.550
No way are we going to stand for this!

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:28.010
What's that?

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:29.340
Don't tell me--

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.300
Brother!

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.220
First High students
victimized by another accident?

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:39.560
Those folks are certainly
disaster-prone, yes?

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.060
Shall I take it upon myself
to exorcise them?

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:50.320
Just as we planned, First High
will now have no choice but to forfeit.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.780
But that's not in the bag just yet.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:57.910
This doesn't change the fact
that First High is still the frontrunner.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:01.580
The Nine Schools Competition
is not just a mere tournament.

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:05.250
It's a major event that captures
the whole world's attention.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:09.670
That's why the wagers have skyrocketed.

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:12.260
If the favorite, First High, were to win,

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:15.300
our losses would exceed
a hundred million dollars.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:20.770
If that happens, it'll be game over
for the No-Head Dragon East Japan Branch.

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:24.230
Not one of us here
will die an easy death.

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:28.820
We have to stop First High School
from winning, no matter what.

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:11.880
U-Um...

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:13.630
Honoka... Satomi...

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:15.170
Yes?

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:20.050
Just because it's the final doesn't mean
it'll be a whole different battle.

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:24.140
If nothing else,
Mirage Bat is a test of stamina.

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:25.890
Right!

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:31.520
My brother is acting like he always does
so they won't get even more nervous.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:34.070
I suppose I have a long way to go.

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:35.900
My brother is absolutely right.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:39.570
What you need more than anything
is to stay calm and pace yourselves.

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:40.990
Am I right?

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:46.580
Yes. All you two have to think about
is how to maximize your natural abilities.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:50.080
You'll be fine. That one-two finish
is ours for the taking.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:52.790
Right!

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:57.550
Mirage Bat Rookie Event Final!
The match is on!

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:04.850
That's our Honoka!

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:07.600
I'm getting the next one!

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:13.270
Both Honoka and Subaru are in fine form!

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:16.070
Of course it's true
that they're in the groove,

00:04:16.070 --> 00:04:18.700
but don't forget that
since Tatsuya adjusted their CADs,

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:22.240
they can process
magic sequences superfast!

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:25.120
So, either one of them
has a chance to win it all!

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:27.580
"Maximize your natural abilities."

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:30.370
I heard Tatsuya say that.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:36.050
And true to his word, he's been supporting us
so that we can draw out our natural abilities.

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:37.510
He did it for Honoka and Subaru.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.010
And for me, as well.

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:44.300
Right! If it weren't for Tatsuya,
I never could've come this far, either.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:47.100
And we're all grateful
to Tatsuya, aren't we?

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:48.520
Yes.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:54.270
I'd like you to tell that
to my brother directly.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:56.520
I'm sure he'll be thrilled!

00:04:58.150 --> 00:04:59.900
Match over!

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:09.240
"ROOKIE EVENT - FINAL"
"HONOKA MITSUI"
"SUBARU SATOMI"

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:04.160
Winner, Honoka Mitsui of First High School!

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:09.500
Runner-up, Subaru Satomi,
also of First High School!

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:10.620
We did it!

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:12.500
Congrats, Honoka!

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:15.590
Tatsuya's prediction came true, huh?

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:17.090
Tatsuya!

00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:18.710
We did it!

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:32.390
What? Tatsuya's competing
in Monolith Code?

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:33.940
Well, after Morisaki's team's accident,

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:37.400
we thought we'd be
withdrawing from Monolith Code...

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:42.200
but the Student Council president seems intent
on winning the Rookie Event, as well.

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:45.660
And that's why she's sending
Tatsuya in as a substitute?

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:57.540
It's true that you'd be more than
competent as a player, too, Brother...

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:00.130
but why does it have to be you?

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:02.630
I argued that point myself.

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:07.140
Why would they pick me, an engineer,
when there are other players to choose from?

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:11.100
And wouldn't there be
long-lasting resentment afterwards?

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:12.350
But...

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:16.940
Don't give me that, Shiba!

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:20.110
You're already a member of the team.

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:23.400
And our leader, Saegusa,
has already chosen you.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:28.280
As a team member, you shouldn't think twice
about following our leader's decisions.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:29.530
Don't try to get out of this, Shiba.

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:34.830
Reserve or not, as long as
you've been chosen, do your job!

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:39.630
They really made it hard for me
to turn them down, so I didn't.

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:40.710
Does that worry you?

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:45.550
If it were just a matter of you competing
in Monolith Code, I wouldn't be worried at all.

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:49.180
The problem is...

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:53.310
The acts of sabotage
against First High, right?

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:56.810
Who on earth is behind all that?

00:06:56.810 --> 00:06:59.860
I'm sure you must know
something, Brother!

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:05.150
A Hong Kong-based crime syndicate,
No-Head Dragon.

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:08.910
They're the ones who inflicted
all of the sabotage we've seen.

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:16.080
Morisaki and his team's injuries...
Was that just an accident?

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.830
What do you mean?

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:22.300
Are you saying it wasn't an accident
but a malicious act of sabotage?

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:24.800
I-I wouldn't go that far.

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:28.050
But it's all too crazy to be a coincidence.

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:29.510
On top of that false start,

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:33.770
use of Battering Ram,
a Rank A Lethal Spell indoors...

00:07:33.770 --> 00:07:37.390
That was no accident.
There's no question that it was deliberate.

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:42.270
But Fourth High was disqualified for using it.

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:44.730
So it did them no good, right?

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:47.030
You do have a point.

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:49.910
Maybe Fourth High was only being used.

00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:52.080
And the real culprit is someone else?

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:55.750
Someone who has no qualms
about maliciously sabotaging First High?

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:57.000
Yeah.

00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:00.710
Tatsuya's taking part
in Monolith Code tomorrow, right?

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:03.170
If something like today
were to happen again--

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:04.550
Don't!

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:06.670
Now that it's come to this...

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:14.010
Why would No-Head Dragon
only come after First High?

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:16.060
What would their purpose be?

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:19.690
I don't know yet, but one thing is clear.

00:08:19.690 --> 00:08:22.730
They don't want First High to win.

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:30.570
Doesn't this mean there's a chance
that they'll go after you again?

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:35.700
Probably. That's why if we defaulted,
we'd be playing right into their hands.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:40.040
If I'm their new target,
then I'll just have to thwart them myself.

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:42.830
Still...

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:49.470
I know you'll be fine, Brother.

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:53.550
I believe that, yet I'm still worried.

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:56.560
If only I could help you somehow.

00:08:57.850 --> 00:08:59.180
Miyuki!

00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:05.230
So, long story short...

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:08.030
let's all protect Tatsuya together!

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:09.280
Yeah!

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:11.740
Uh, what's going on?

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:15.830
Miyuki, we're sure that today's
Monolith Code accident

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:20.370
was deliberate sabotage
by someone targeting First High.

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:27.630
So, we're thinking that Tatsuya and the team
will be targeted in tomorrow's match.

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:32.550
Since Tatsuya went above and beyond
for us in our Rookie Events...

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:36.510
we've been thinking
about what we could do to thank him.

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:38.890
And that's how this strategy was born!

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:40.180
OPERATION REPAY TATSUYA FOR HIS KINDNESS!

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:43.310
After always supporting us
from behind the scenes,

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:45.520
Tatsuya will be taking
center stage as a player!

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:48.070
Now it's our turn to support him!

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:52.150
OPERATION REPAY TATSUYA FOR HIS KINDNESS!

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:52.070
So, these are the three possible scenarios
for sabotage that we can think of!

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:54.110
ANTICIPATED ACTS OF SABOTAGE

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:54.110
*DIRECT EXTERNAL ATTACK DURING THE MATCH

00:09:54.490 --> 00:09:58.580
The Tournament Committee
is strict about checking the CADs,

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:01.370
which we can't do anything about,

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:04.670
so we came up with countermeasures
for the other two.

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:07.590
Security's supposed to be tight
during the match,

00:10:07.590 --> 00:10:10.840
but that still didn't stop
what happened today.

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:14.130
They check the five stages in advance,

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:18.510
but if their aim is sabotage, of course
they'd make sure it would go undetected.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:24.190
So, before the match starts,
we're going to do safety checks on the stages.

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:28.020
And then, we'll be patrolling the venue
during the match!

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:31.280
That will be our mission for the day!

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:33.280
What do you think, Miyuki?

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:37.030
Thank you, everyone.
For my brother's sake.

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:39.620
I'd be happy to take part, as well.

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:43.410
But I do have two favors to ask of you.

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:44.250
Huh?

00:10:44.250 --> 00:10:48.630
First, I'd like to keep this
a secret from my brother.

00:10:48.630 --> 00:10:51.800
If he found out that we were doing
something behind his back,

00:10:51.800 --> 00:10:53.840
I'm sure he'd be concerned.

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:55.470
One more thing.

00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:57.680
Just don't do anything dangerous.

00:10:57.680 --> 00:11:01.810
If you were to get injured,
my brother would be distressed.

00:11:01.810 --> 00:11:02.890
Right.

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:06.100
Substitutes?

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:07.230
What should we do?

00:11:07.230 --> 00:11:12.110
If First High's the only school to get
into another accident, it'd invite suspicion!

00:11:12.110 --> 00:11:16.950
Don't worry. All we have to do
is prevent First High from winning.

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:19.570
There are other ways, too.

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:39.010
FIRST HIGH SCHOOL

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:39.010
AUGUST 10, 2095 - MONOLITH CODE - ROOKIE EVENT - FINAL DAY

00:11:41.350 --> 00:11:43.850
What's wrong, Eimi?
Didn't get enough sleep?

00:11:43.850 --> 00:11:45.350
Ah, no.

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:48.100
I got up early to check the stage.

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:49.310
Hey!

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:52.110
N-N-Nothing! It's nothing!

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:55.820
Brother...

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:57.700
Good luck.

00:11:57.700 --> 00:11:59.360
Right.

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:01.370
Well, substitute or not,

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:03.870
since I've been chosen,
I have to give it my all, right?

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:05.700
Let's go, Mikihiko.

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:07.710
I'll just do whatever I can.

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:15.880
Okay, you guys!

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:17.470
Let's stick to the plan!

00:12:17.470 --> 00:12:18.300
Right!

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:21.340
2095 NATIONAL MAGIC HIGH SCHOOL GOODWILL
 TOURNAMENT OF MAGIC SKILLS

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:22.390
Is that you, Miyuki?

00:12:22.390 --> 00:12:25.770
Fujibayashi!
I didn't know you'd be here.

00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:27.600
Yes, I'm here for work,

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:32.730
but that means I'll get to see the showdown
between Tatsuya and the Crimson Prince.

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:35.530
Crimson Prince?

00:12:35.530 --> 00:12:37.990
You mean the heir apparent
to the Ichijo Family?

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:41.910
His Magic Burst
is a powerful spell, you know.

00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:45.410
But I'm sure Tatsuya can handle it just fine!

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:47.540
No matter who his opponent is...

00:12:47.540 --> 00:12:50.170
there's no way my brother could lose.

00:12:51.630 --> 00:12:53.540
Please stay safe.

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:18.610
Game over!

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:21.200
Winner, First High School!

00:13:22.410 --> 00:13:25.200
Congratulations, Brother!

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:28.240
"ROOKIE EVENT"
"QUALIFYING ROUND"
"THIRD HIGH SCHOOL VS FIRST HIGH SCHOOL"

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:32.870
Wow, they all look delicious!

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:39.170
91 Ice Cream has flavors
you can only get here, so you should try it.

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:38.790
{=0}ICE CREAM

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:43.010
I can see how coming here every year
gives you the inside track!

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:48.310
Ah, just as I thought, it's you, yes?

00:13:48.310 --> 00:13:51.390
Hey! Please don't just
sneak up and touch me!

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:55.520
Forgive me. Next time,
I'll give you a shout before I touch you.

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:57.360
That's not acceptable, either!

00:13:57.360 --> 00:14:01.400
We had the pleasure of watching
Tatsuya Shiba's match earlier.

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:04.490
Who knew that he was capable
of using Gram Demolition?

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:07.240
His teammates also acquitted
themselves well.

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:13.080
The biggest mystery is
why they were reserves with all that talent.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:16.590
Is that for fencing?

00:14:16.590 --> 00:14:19.670
Yes. I was using it to practice
for tomorrow's Mirage Bat.

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:20.880
Airi.

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:26.680
It doesn't matter. They couldn't surpass
my speed even if they found out my strategy.

00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:30.350
I'm going to win tomorrow's match.

00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:35.270
Still, what's ailing this place?
'Tis so unpleasant, yes?

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:36.100
What?

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:38.190
Can you not sense it, too?

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:41.280
The spirits are strangely restless.

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:45.740
Down below, yes?

00:14:45.740 --> 00:14:49.410
As a Light Element,
I'd wager that you can see them.

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:55.830
These are spirits?

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:59.170
This isn't how normal spirits move.

00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:03.550
This presence here belongs
to Ancient Magic from the Continent.

00:15:03.550 --> 00:15:05.930
Ancient Magic from the Continent?

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:12.060
Most likely, someone must've set this up
to control these spirits.

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:14.640
Could this be for sabotage?

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:16.560
Sabotage?

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:18.440
Whatever do you mean?

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:24.110
Using spirits
to manipulate the ley lines?

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:27.450
Yes, but we don't know
why they'd do that.

00:15:27.450 --> 00:15:32.330
The spirits' power is weak, so the most they
could accomplish by manipulating the ley lines

00:15:32.330 --> 00:15:35.330
would be to let the water seep out a bit.

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:40.340
So, muddying it or generating fog
wouldn't cause significant interference.

00:15:40.340 --> 00:15:45.300
Would you go out of your way to use
Ancient Magic from the Continent for that?

00:15:45.300 --> 00:15:47.630
Water...

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:50.760
Before the match starts, water...

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:52.890
Water...

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:54.060
Surely not!

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:55.810
Magic Burst?

00:15:55.810 --> 00:16:01.270
The Ichijo Family's spell, Magic Burst,
vaporizes liquids and causes explosions.

00:16:01.270 --> 00:16:03.190
The ley lines that seep out
into the arena...

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:08.070
are all just like explosives to him!

00:16:08.070 --> 00:16:12.580
Then, is this Ancient Magic being used
to give Third High an advantage?

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:16.870
'Tisn't us! As if we would ever
stoop to such low tactics!

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:18.670
Right. I know that.

00:16:18.670 --> 00:16:21.460
The enemy's goal is to prevent
First High from winning.

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:24.880
And they're trying to let
Third High win to achieve that.

00:16:24.880 --> 00:16:26.210
Enemy?

00:16:39.940 --> 00:16:42.730
Th-This is the Ichijo Family's...

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:45.230
Magic Burst?

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:52.870
Apparently, the goddess of fate
wants me to win.

00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:54.910
Honoka, get over here
as fast as you can!

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:58.830
Before they face off against Third High,
we have to fix whatever they did to the stage!

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:00.370
Gotcha!

00:17:02.170 --> 00:17:07.130
We didn't know
you'd been dragged into all that.

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:10.340
I did think that First High
was getting into too many accidents,

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:12.140
but who knew it was sabotage?

00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:16.100
So, it was the same with that bus accident
and the Battle Board incident, too?

00:17:16.100 --> 00:17:21.060
We didn't make that connection
ourselves at first, but probably.

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:22.650
How diabolical!

00:17:22.650 --> 00:17:24.060
The Nine Schools Competition

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:28.530
is a place for magicians of the same
generation to clash at full power.

00:17:28.530 --> 00:17:30.950
For them to dare to sabotage that...

00:17:34.070 --> 00:17:35.280
Honoka...

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:38.870
Can you pass on the information
that you see to me?

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:39.870
Yes.

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:52.300
There!

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:54.930
I'll stop the ley lines in their tracks!

00:17:59.270 --> 00:18:02.020
Let's move on!
There are still four stages to go!

00:18:02.020 --> 00:18:03.230
We'd better hurry!

00:18:03.230 --> 00:18:04.730
Right!

00:18:06.690 --> 00:18:08.190
Who are you?

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:16.740
Leave this to me!

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:19.040
You move on to the Open Plains Stage!

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:22.120
The Forest Stage and the Gorge Stage
are taken care of.

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:24.420
Thanks to my Spirit Magic, that is!

00:18:24.420 --> 00:18:27.460
Why would you Third High students...

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:31.050
The Nine Schools Competition
is all about us players

00:18:31.050 --> 00:18:34.760
settling scores fair and square
through our matches.

00:18:34.760 --> 00:18:36.550
Isn't that right?

00:18:38.140 --> 00:18:40.600
Isshiki, thank you.

00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:43.440
If you want to thank me,
I'll be all ears after this is over.

00:18:43.440 --> 00:18:44.940
Now get going!

00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:46.480
Very well!

00:18:58.780 --> 00:18:59.990
This battleground...

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:03.580
belongs to us students and no one else!

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:06.420
You people have no right to take part!

00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:24.270
We did it, huh, Miyuki?

00:19:24.270 --> 00:19:25.560
Yes.

00:19:29.940 --> 00:19:32.610
What should we do with these people?

00:19:32.610 --> 00:19:35.070
Shall we make them give up who they are?

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:37.990
They probably won't say a word.

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:41.160
Not with ordinary torture.

00:19:41.160 --> 00:19:43.040
If that's what you're planning...

00:19:43.040 --> 00:19:45.040
can you let me take care of it?

00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:47.000
Fujibayashi!

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:48.170
You know each other?

00:19:48.170 --> 00:19:49.790
Y-Yes.

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:52.960
Just leave the dirty work to us grown-ups.

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:54.880
Now head back.

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:57.970
Or Tatsuya's match will start without you.

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:03.180
Who on earth is she?

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:05.930
Hey, don't you think we look silly...

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:07.440
in these outfits?

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:10.560
I can just see Erika
laughing her head off.

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:12.150
I know, right?

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:20.990
What's wrong, Tatsuya?

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:25.370
Apparently, we can't afford
to lose this match.

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:29.790
The Monolith Code Rookie Event Final!

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:34.750
The match between First High School
and Third High School is about to begin!

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:37.300
First High School's victory...

00:20:37.300 --> 00:20:39.130
is all but a dead certainty now!

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:42.600
At this point, we'll have to use
whatever methods we can!

00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:47.430
We'll have the First High player default
during tomorrow's Mirage Bat Event.

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:49.520
Forcibly, that is.

00:20:56.570 --> 00:20:58.700
Didn't I tell you before?

00:20:58.700 --> 00:21:00.910
You and I are enemies.

00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:03.330
You can thank me later.

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:07.040
Right. And I must tell you
that this isn't thanks.

00:21:07.040 --> 00:21:09.660
It's my declaration of war.

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:11.670
During tomorrow's Mirage Bat Event...

00:21:11.670 --> 00:21:14.540
I will play you fair and square,
going all out...

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:17.380
and I will defeat you.

00:21:17.380 --> 00:21:19.260
I'll be looking forward to that.

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:37.690
"FIRST HIGH SCHOOL"

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:41.360
Winner of the Monolith Code
Rookie Event, First High School!

00:21:48.580 --> 00:21:49.870
Brother!
